 succeeded in 7019ms:
22430: ### `cxlaunchwallfp` (LOW, harness) — cxlaunch.sh reports a complete codex answer as WALLED, two ways
22431: 
22432: On 2026-09-26 the launcher printed `*** SEAT WALLED.` for the `#550` and `#549` Astra confirmations, and both answers
22433: were complete (`CONFIRM WITH CHANGES`, 4.3 KB and 11.5 KB).  **Two different false positives:** (1) `#550`'s stderr held
22434: six `^ERROR: You've hit your usage limit` lines that were an OLDER session's output file, echoed while codex read it --
22435: they start at column 0, so the file's own `^ERROR:` anchor cannot tell them from codex's diagnostics; (2) `#549`'s stdout
22436: matched `quota` inside the word "quotation".  The file's header already records this class (a quoted marker re-arms the
22437: tool that reads it).  Fix shape: key the stderr test on codex's own error block at the END of the stream, and give the
22438: stdout patterns word boundaries; negative-control both directions (a real wall still reds; these two runs do not).
22439: Found while confirming `#550`.
22440: 
22441: ## 2026-09-25 — GXEMUL [087a90]: `#551` wdcidselfcheck; what its review files
22442: 
22443: Evidence: `regress/artifacts/wdcidselfcheck_20260925/` -- eight panels (codex walled on every one: a seat failure,
22444: re-fired after 2026-09-26 07:01), the Opus records and measurements, the dedicated grok jobs, and the Fable 5.1
22445: adjudications of both F2 passes and of the `#551d`, `#551e` and `#551f` passes (the chain closed on `#551f`'s).
22446: 
22447: ### `panelwallquote` (MED, harness) — panel.sh's seat check reads an answer that QUOTES "usage limit" as a wall
22448: 
22449: On `#551`'s F2 panel (`panel_20260925_144647`), `panel.sh`'s seat check printed minimax's COMPLETE answer -- four
22450: numbered items and a verdict line -- as `*** WALLED MID-ANSWER ***`, because the answer quoted the brief's own sentence
22451: about codex's "usage limit".  `tools/pipeline/seat_verdicts.py`, which keys on WHERE a notice sits, reads the same file
22452: as answered (PROCEED WITH CHANGES).  This is the carrier's quoted-marker class re-arming a tool, in the check that tells
22453: the operator to re-fire a seat: the cost is a wasted re-fire, or -- worse -- a real wall discounted as "probably the
22454: quote again".  `panel.sh` carries unreviewed working-tree deltas and is not committed as-is, so its round starts from
22455: them.  The fix is the one `seat_verdicts.py` already has: key on the notice's position, never on the phrase alone,
22456: with two negative controls -- an answer that quotes the phrase stays answered; a real mid-answer wall still reds.
22457: **A second instance, the opposite direction:** on every panel from `panel_20260925_160838`, codex's 831-byte file -- the
22458: CLI banner, the prompt, and two `ERROR: You've hit your usage limit` lines -- is flagged `WALLED MID-ANSWER` in its
22459: detail line and then counted among the seats that "produced output" in the SEATS summary, which names only kimi as
22460: unanswered.  A reader of the summary line sees codex as answered.  Same fix: the summary counts what the detail line
22461: classified, never the byte count.
22462: 
22463: ### `wdcidcomparators` (MED, detector) — 104 of diff_wdc_identify.c's 128 rows compare where the self-check does not reach
22464: 
22465: `#551` gave `regress/diff_wdc_identify.c` a self-check on its two comparators, `chk()` and a new device-independent `row_cmp()`, and
22466: the file's LAST self-check pins its comparator call counts (`chk()` 24, `row_cmp()` 8, `#551f`).  Only 24 rows compare
22467: INSIDE a comparator the self-check feeds (16 `chk()` got/want calls and 8 `row_cmp()` calls); 8 more hand `chk()` a 0/1
22468: verdict computed at the call (derive: `grep -cE '\? [01] : [01], 1\);' regress/diff_wdc_identify.c`), so a verdict
22469: computation that goes inert is invisible to the self-check; the other 96 compare INLINE.  Owner ruling 2026-09-25: "24/128
22470: now, file the rest".  The route (the Fable 5.1 ruling on `#551`, item 5): move the inline and verdict rows onto
22471: comparators the self-check feeds, with the measured requirements `#551` met as the bar -- the original row output kept,
22472: adding only the SELFCHECK lines and the covered-failure report lines (four on `w57hi`, five on `w58lo`), at -O2 and
22473: -O0, across the seven `dev_wdc.c` variants; every vacuity control red.  (This said "byte-identical stdout except the
22474: SELFCHECK lines", which `#551` did not meet: its report lines are measured additions, `measured/run551f.out` section
22475: 2 -- GPT-6 Astra, confirming `#551`.)  Also owed here,
22476: disclosed by `#551` and measured (`wdcidselfcheck_20260925/measured/run551v2.out`, variant `rows`): a rows- or name-keyed
22477: test inside either comparator, placed before its `rows ++`, keeps every gate-2 row green while silencing any covered row
