  108:     to change the tallies by exactly the right amount -- including each `row_cmp()` disjunct wrong alone with got ABOVE
  109:     its want and `sectors` 0, so `<` for `!=` and an added `&& sectors` are red; the G text printed ONCE, by the last
  110:     run, only when both passed; a self-check that did not pass counts one failure in the trailer; and the LAST one pins
  111:     the runtime call counts, `chk()` 24 and `row_cmp()` 8;
  112:   * `cmp_fails`: the comparators count their own failures and the trailer reports the larger count, so a `failures =
  113:     0;` after the covered rows no longer turns the run green;
  114:   * **the covered-failure report (`#551f`)**: on a non-probe mismatch each comparator prints
  115:     `  FAIL  covered comparator failure -- N failures so far`, a line gate 2's `[0-9]+ failures` check reads at the
  116:     moment it fails -- so once it is in the log no later edit of the tallies, the trailer or the rows' order takes it
  117:     back (`lib.sh`'s `check()` compares the newline-joined list of EVERY captured number with the one string `0`,
  118:     so any extra match reds it, even one reading `0 failures`);
  119:   * **the contract**, a partition of where an in-file edit can act: (A) the comparators are pinned; (B) a covered
  120:     failure reports itself; (C) observables forged; (D) the block itself -- under a boundary paragraph saying what
  121:     every in-file check can and cannot see, and what crosses it (filed: `wdcidlane`).
