906: #
907: #  This was `git status --porcelain`, i.e. staged AND unstaged together.  That is correct for a
908: #  single-writer session and WRONG the moment two rounds run in parallel: on 2026-08-21 a
909: #  records-only commit (tools/ and OUTSTANDING_BUGS only) was blocked by sections A and B firing
910: #  on `src/machines/machine_hpcmips.c` -- a file a CONCURRENT agent was editing and had not yet
911: #  propagated, and which the commit did not touch.
912: #
913: #  Nothing is weakened by the narrowing.  The un-propagated file is still caught -- at the moment
914: #  it is committed, because then it IS staged.  What changes is that it no longer blocks an
915: #  unrelated commit, which is the difference between a gate and an obstacle.
916: #
917: #  The fallback matters: with nothing staged (an interactive run, or `git commit -a`), fall back
918: #  to the full working tree, so a bare invocation still audits everything.  A check that silently
919: #  audited nothing when run the ordinary way would be worse than the problem being fixed.
920: CHANGED=$(git diff --cached --name-only)
