70: PANEL_RE = re.compile(r"panel_\d{8}_\d{6}")
71: 
72: 
73: #  *** A CITED DIR WITH A DESCRIPTIVE SUFFIX WAS SILENTLY UNVERIFIABLE UNTIL 2026-08-25. ***
74: #  PANEL_RE extracts the bare `panel_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` stem, but real panel dirs often carry a
108: def cited_pairs(ledger):
109:     """(panel_dir, seat) and (panel_dir, filename) the ledger claims, plus the dirs in scope.
110: 
111:     A file is counted as read if the entry NAMES IT, or -- for a seat with only one answer
112:     file in that directory -- if the entry cites the directory and the seat.  The filename
113:     form is what closes the two-answers-one-citation hole; the seat form is kept so older
114:     entries that cite a directory without a filename still count.
115:     """
116:     pairs, files, dirs = set(), set(), set()
117:     for row in ledger["rows"]:
118:         for ent in row.get("entries", []):
119:             blob = "%s %s" % (ent.get("ev", ""), ent.get("note", ""))
120:             for d in PANEL_RE.findall(blob):
121:                 dirs.add(d)
122:                 pairs.add((d, ent.get("seat")))
123:                 for fn in FILE2SEAT:
124:                     if fn in blob:
125:                         files.add((d, fn))
126:     return pairs, files, dirs
127: 

codex
The main correction is to L1’s filing scope: four of the “fifteen unbuilt” reset shapes already have builds and saved results in the later M18 artifacts. I also found that merely citing these `panels/` directories will not put the re-fired answers under section G: its matcher requires timestamped panel names and a fixed list of answer filenames. Both are record corrections; neither shows a new false pass by the shipped detector.
